+        # The HF-bridge checkpoint path (save_contents without "optimizer") never restores the
+        # LR scheduler or the Adam moments. On resume: (1) fast-forward the scheduler so the
+        # decay matches an uninterrupted run; (2) ramp the LR linearly over the first
+        # VERL_RESUME_LR_WARMUP_STEPS steps (default 10) so freshly initialised Adam moments do
+        # not produce full-size sign-like updates (observed: loss 0.23 -> 0.78 after one step).
